<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Kim Isabu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabu, or Kim Isabu, was a general of Silla in the 6th century. In 512 he subdued the island state of Usan (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulleungdo">Ulleungdo</a>), reputedly by threatening to release wooden lions, and in 562 he conquered Daegaya, the last of the Gaya states, with the young hwarang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadaham">Sadaham</a>. In 545 he proposed the compilation of a national history of Silla.</p></div>
